# Database Domain

## Tenancy (multi-league IHL)

- **Game** — catalog row (`id`, `displayName`). Example: `warcraft3_udbr`.
- **League** — one IHL instance: `(guildId, gameId, name)` unique. Holds per-IHL settings (wc3stats, leaderboard channel ids, lobby claim flag). Default league created per guild during migration/backfill.
- **LeagueChannelBinding** — maps a Discord channel or category (`discordId`, `kind`) to a `leagueId`. Used by `resolveLeagueContext`.
- **GuildConfig** — guild-wide only: create/mod role ids, claim defaults at guild level where still used. **Not** wc3stats or leaderboard (those live on `League`).

Ratings and matches **never** cross `leagueId`. `Player.username` / `Player.discordId` stay **globally** unique (one Discord link across all leagues).

## Tables

- **Player** — `username` (battletag/nick); optional `discordId` (Ghost Profile)
- **PlayerRating** — League-scoped overall skill (μ/σ). PK `(leagueId, playerId)`
- **Hero** — IDs 1–12, tied to lobby slots (WC3 UDBR catalog; not universal for future games)
- **PlayerHeroRating** — League-scoped hero μ/σ + `matchesPlayed`. PK `(leagueId, playerId, heroId)`
- **Match** — Up to 6v6 sessions; required `leagueId`; status (unbalanced fills allowed)
- **MatchPlayer** — team, slot, hero, result
- **LeagueWc3statsSlotMap** — `game:warcraft3_udbr` slot layout. PK `(leagueId, wc3statsSlot)`

## Design Decisions

- Username is the primary player identifier (not Discord ID)
- Overall vs hero ratings live in separate tables (SRP); both scoped by `leagueId`
- Lobby has 12 slots: 1–6 = Team A, 7–12 = Team B; slot ID = hero ID (UDBR)
- Full lobby is 6v6; asymmetric human fills (e.g. 4v6, 5v3) are valid if both teams have ≥1 player
- `MatchResult` may include DRAW, but the game only uses WIN/LOSS
- Active wc3stats game id uniqueness is per `leagueId`, not process-wide
- Ranking math / ordinal / quitters: see `openskill-rating.mdc`
